WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:14.490
Inside tile, left and right are FP16 matrix fragments and sum is an FP32 accumulator fragment. fill_fragment sets the initial accumulator; the loads use a row stride of 16 elements.

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:20.400
All 32 threads call the same warp-wide operations with matching pointers and parameters.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.195
Load fragments.

00:00:23.195 --> 00:00:25.560
The warp supplies A and B operands.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.730
Matrix multiply-accumulate.

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:31.015
Combine operands with the existing accumulator.

00:00:31.015 --> 00:00:32.350
Store the tile.

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:34.900
Write the updated accumulator to C.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:40.585
Tensor cores are matrix execution units inside an SM.

00:00:40.585 --> 00:00:45.455
A warp collectively supplies register fragments for matrix instructions.

00:00:45.455 --> 00:00:52.525
WMMA’s fragment layout is device-dependent; a source tile is not a diagram of individual tensor-core units.
